Aerie-Purpose: List each install of a browser once in the setup page's import step: Flatpak installs of Chromium-family browsers and Helium get a row, Flatpak rows say so, and a source that is listed twice is listed once.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/importer (chrome_importer_list.cc, importer_list.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #91. Helium's importer list (Brave's chrome_importer_list.cc) looks only at native
Chromium-family folders under ~/.config, so a Flatpak Chromium (org.chromium.Chromium, whose data
is in ~/.var/app/<id>/config/chromium) and Helium itself were never offered. On Linux
DetectChromeProfiles now also tries the folders aerie_import_sources::ExtraChromiumSources lists, and
DetectSourceProfilesWorker passes the finished list through NormalizeSources: a Flatpak source gets
" (Flatpak)" after its name so it reads apart from the native install, and a source with the same
importer type and the same folder (symlinks resolved, as with Zen's second Flatpak id) is listed once.
Both files include import_sources.h and take the home directory from it. Helium has no importer type; its profile has Chromium's format, so it imports as Chrome.

